 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Class InterleaveIterator(arrays, cycle). Elements are produced round-robin: element 0 of each array in array order, then element 1 of each array that has one, and so on; exhausted and empty arrays are skipped. With cycle false the iterator ends after one pass. With cycle true the whole interleaved sequence restarts from the beginning after it is exhausted, forever, unless there are no elements at all. hasNext() reports whether next() would produce a value; next() returns the next value, or null when none is available (inference).",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk03-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
